<%# Shared curl example of the Gatekeeper labs. Include it with the curl view (see curlFor in lab.ts). Every value goes through the escaped output tag. Never put an EJS tag inside an EJS comment: it breaks parsing. %>
<p class="lab-note">From a terminal: <code>curl "<%= curl.url %>"<% curl.headers.forEach(function (h) { %> -H "<%= h %>"<% }); %> -b "hvwa_sid=&lt;copy from devtools&gt;<% curl.cookies.forEach(function (c) { %>; <%= c %><% }); %>"<% if (curl.data) { %> -d '<%= curl.data %>'<% } %></code>. Your lab belongs to your browser session: sign in here first, then copy the (HttpOnly) <code>hvwa_sid</code> cookie from the devtools storage into <code>-b</code>. Without it curl starts a different session, and its state and flags will not match yours.</p>
